Subject: [PATCH 3/3] MemoryCore: operator commands for planning and applying forgetting

Adds `forget plan` / `forget apply` / `forget audit`, thin wrappers around the
engine in this repository. Deliberately not a background job: the first adoption
should be a human reading a plan and typing `apply`. A scheduler can come later,
once the plan has been reviewed a few times and the thresholds are calibrated
against a real corpus rather than a guessed default.

Structure of the change:
  MemoryCore/src/cli/commands/forget.ts   the three subcommands
  MemoryCore/src/cli/index.ts             register them

Both wrap src/cli.ts of tdai-forgetting, kept as a sibling package so the engine's
tests run without the full gateway build. Once the policy stabilises, the engine
can be inlined into MemoryCore and the wrapper deleted.
